{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>A permanent servant.</b> One might think literally so; therefore Scripture states, ״וְשַׁבְתֶּם אִישׁ אֶל אֲחֻזָּתוֹ וְאִישׁ אֶל מִשְׁפַּחְתּוֹ תָּשֻׁבוּ״ (Leviticus 25) — thus you learn that this is only until the Jubilee (Mekhilta, Exodus 21)." "<b>And likewise you shall do for your maidservant.</b> Give her a gift; one might think the verse equated her also for piercing — therefore Scripture states (Exodus 21), ״וְאִם אָמֹר יֹאמַר הָעֶבֶד״ — a male servant is pierced, but a maidservant is not pierced (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:15.354785472Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}